  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency food security and livelihood support for IDPs and host comunities in Aloz locality</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to improve food security and livelihoods recovery for the Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) and host communities in 4 villages in Algoz locality, South Kordofan. The focus of the project is on increasing food productivity  as well as improving animals condition for targeted people and communities. This will be done through:
1. Provision of agricultural inputs and services (seeds, equipment and training) for 1500 farmers.
2. Improvement of livestock quality for 1000 households, through vaccination campaigns.
3. Conducting refresher training for10 Community Animal Health Workers-the CAHWs
4. Providing livestock (goats) to 5 most vulnerable families. 
The project will be implemented for 12 months. CAFOD will be working with a National Partner SIDO. The project funding is through Sudan Humanitarian Funds (SHF), with collaboration of other six  NGOs each working in different localities.</narrative>
  </description>
